Found it. The page loads **MDBootstrap** (`mdb.min.css`), whose `.badge` rule forces white text (with `!important`). My original `color` declaration wasn't marked `!important`, so the white won and the "Workshop" text was white-on-transparent — invisible.

I've added `!important` to the workshop badge's text color, and confirmed it's now in the compiled, live stylesheet:

```684:689:_sass/_base.scss
        abbr.workshop {
          background-color: transparent !important;
          color: var(--global-theme-color) !important;
          border: 1px solid var(--global-theme-color);
          margin-left: 0.4rem;
        }
```

Do a hard refresh (Cmd+Shift+R) on `http://localhost:4000/publications/` and the "Workshop" label should now show in the theme color inside the outlined box. If you'd prefer it more prominent, I can switch it to a filled gray/neutral pill with white text instead of the outlined style.

